# Line endings.
#
# Git's default on Windows is core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout. That changes the bytes on disk, and tests/test_reference_is_frozen.py
# asserts the sha256 of five files under reference/ -- so on a Windows runner all
# five failed with "has been MODIFIED", for a change git made rather than a
# person. Every file in this repository is LF; keep it LF in the working tree
# on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The parity oracle is evidence, and its bytes are not to be translated by
# anything, for any reason. That is exactly what the checksum test asserts, so
# say it here too rather than relying on the rule above.
reference/** -text
